BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:6000+ Declarations of Independence
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260601
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTSTAMP:20261029T171815Z
UID:0388aaee98d57b621b5de147acef@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Through original comic art by artist Joe Young and historical 
 storytelling\, this exhibit explores how Black abolitionists claimed freed
 om\, dignity\, and humanity in a nation that denied them all three. Center
 ing the lives and writings of figures including Frederick Douglass\, Harri
 et Jacobs\, Sojourner Truth\, and Josiah Henson\, the exhibition examines 
 storytelling as both resistance and liberation.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit
 .com/events/6000-declarations-independence
LOCATION:Stowe Center for Literary Activism\, 77 Forest Street\, Hartford 
 CT\, 06105
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/6000-declarations-independence
END:VEVENT
