DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTSTAMP:20261029T171815Z
UID:465dfea13e4a4aa3e597ed2df6e2@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:How can art communicate what words sometimes cannot? Join a Cu
 ratorial Team member at the Mattatuck Museum\, along with Briana Benn Mira
 ndi\, art therapist from Art and Soul Art Therapy in Madison\, for a conve
 rsation exploring mental health\, the benefits of art therapy\, and our ex
 hibition Franne Davids and the World She Painted. The panel will explore h
 ow art allows us to express emotions\, experiences\, and ideas beyond spok
 en and written language\, while supporting emotional well-being and deepen
 ing our understanding of ourselves and one another.\n\nSource: https://ctv
 isit.com/events/cocktails-conversations-language-art-expression-healing-co
 nnection
LOCATION:Mattatuck Museum\, 144 West Main St.\, Waterbury CT\, 06702
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/cocktails-conversations-language-art-expres
 sion-healing-connection
END:VEVENT
